# Do Not Store CardVi or SegVi

See [README CardVi and SegVi](../../README.md#cardvi-and-segvi).

`Widget` fully owns `CardVi` and `SegVi` (create, rebind, collapse/expand detach, destroy). Application and example code must **not** store them as fields, maps, or caches. A held Vi goes stale after collapse, splice, remount, or `Widget.destroy`.

Keep `ICard` / `ISeg`. Look up `card.vis[treeUuid]` or `seg.vis[treeUuid]` at the call site (use `event.widgetTreeUuids.card` or `widget.treeUuids.card`) and drop the reference. Do not import `CardVi` / `SegVi` into app code to stash instances.

Incorrect:

```typescript
class MyController {
  private cardVi: CardVi;
  constructor(card: ICard, treeUuid: string) {
    this.cardVi = card.vis[treeUuid];
  }
}
```

Correct:

```typescript
const vi = card.vis[event.widgetTreeUuids.card];
vi?.htmlElement?.classList.add("...");
```

Framework code inside `xorlab/src/renderer` may hold Vi references. `xorlab-interactive` controllers keep `ICard` (and sometimes `HTMLElement`) and re-read `card.vis[treeUuid]` each time.
